        "original_id": "ea0fb448-1053-5cc4-afaa-bcab45dbd7a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Backpacker murders\n- People: Ivan Milat\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia; Belanglo State Forest; Berrima\n- Organizations: New South Wales Government\n- Topics: Serial killings; pine plantings\n\nFacts:\n- The Backpacker murders were a spate of serial killings that took place in New South Wales, Australia, between 1989 and 1993.\n- Ivan Milat committed the Backpacker murders.\n- The bodies of seven missing young people aged 19 to 22 were discovered partially buried in Belanglo State Forest, 15 km south-west of Berrima in New South Wales.\n- Belanglo State Forest is owned by the New South Wales Government.\n- Belanglo State Forest contains some of the earliest pine plantings in New South Wales.",
